9535801 true] [17592186366953 1113 #uuid "061e6504-cfaf-51e0-88ae-f11dcba1d1dc" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366953 1145 "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=2$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and  III are false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=2>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-3<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, neither the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ nor the matrix $A$ is positive-definite or negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366955 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366956 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366957 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366958 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366959 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1041 "selection" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366956 13194139535801 true] [17592186366954 1110 #uuid "cfd2b46e-3d30-5d11-9f46-beb860994b6f" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366955 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535801 true] [17592186366955 1111 #uuid "fd3c3a8c-4613-5148-9e30-ec1000e66629" 13194139535801 true] [17592186366956 1034 "I only" 13194139535801 true] [175921863